<div class="scene-controls scene-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Choose a timescale" hidden>
  <button type="button" data-time-view-button="sample" aria-pressed="true">Large sample</button>
  <button type="button" data-time-view-button="lens" aria-pressed="false">Lensed LRD</button>
</div>
<svg class="science-svg temporal-svg" viewBox="0 0 520 400" role="img" aria-labelledby="time-title time-desc">
  <title id="time-title">Variability on two timescales</title>
  <desc id="time-desc">
    Two synthetic views. Large sample: 314 little red dots observed at a few epochs over a few years, plotted as the change between epochs against brightness; most lie inside the grey measurement-noise band and eight variable candidates lie above it, with an example light curve below. Lensed LRD: a quasi-periodic pulsation of one source's envelope, seen as four lensed images whose light left the source up to about 130 years apart, with a scrolling light curve marking each image's moment and a few-year JWST band.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <radialGradient id="time-envelope"><stop stop-color="#fff6e8"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#f4b48d" stop-opacity=".95" data-temp-stop/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#f4b48d" stop-opacity=".25" data-temp-stop/></radialGradient>
    <radialGradient id="time-envelope-glow"><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#f4b48d" stop-opacity=".35" data-temp-stop/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#f4b48d" stop-opacity="0" data-temp-stop/></radialGradient>
    <radialGradient id="time-lens"><stop stop-color="#f1dcc0" stop-opacity=".55"/><stop offset=".35" stop-color="#a1abb6" stop-opacity=".22"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#728ba4" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient>
